--- V2 negative check (supplemental) ---
V2 configStorePath blocked: code=16 remark=Can not update config path

--- Mechanism detail ---
Original seed (CVE-2023-33246 nameserver vector):
  UPDATE_NAMESRV_CONFIG (remoting code 318) body: kvConfigPath=/tmp/pcb_marker.txt
  Then PUT_KV_CONFIG (code 100) to store a KV pair with the flag as value.
  KVConfigManager.persist() writes the KV data to the path set in kvConfigPath.
  V0: no blocklist -> write succeeds.
  V1: kvConfigPath in blocklist -> code 16 NO_PERMISSION.

Bypass residual (CVE-2023-37582):
  UPDATE_NAMESRV_CONFIG body: configStorePath=/tmp/pcb_marker.txt\nproductEnvName=<FLAG>
  Configuration.update() sets configStorePath and productEnvName, then calls persist().
  persist() writes the full NamesrvConfig (including productEnvName=<FLAG>) to the new configStorePath.
  V1: configStorePath NOT in blocklist (5.1.1 blocklists 'configStorePathName' not 'configStorePath') -> write succeeds.
  V2: configStorePath IS in blocklist -> code 16 NO_PERMISSION.

--- Root cause of incomplete fix ---
The 5.1.1 nameserver handler contains:
  if (properties.containsKey("kvConfigPath") || properties.containsKey("configStorePathName"))
The property 'configStorePathName' does NOT exist in NamesrvConfig. The real property is 'configStorePath'.
The 5.1.2 fix corrects this to:
  if (properties.containsKey("kvConfigPath") || properties.containsKey("configStorePath"))

--- Container marker file contents ---
V0 /tmp/pcb_marker.txt (KV config):
  {"configTable":{"PCB_CANARY":{"flag":"<FLAG>"}}}

V1 /tmp/pcb_marker.txt (namesrv config):
  ...productEnvName=<FLAG>...configStorePath=/tmp/pcb_marker.txt...
